{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KyEvqNn34L2aaTyXrw89Rp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the three findings. Let me reconsider the key constraint: `@earendil-works/pi-ai` is **not** a build dependency (per `pi/types.ts`), so a real *completing* `ModelCall` cannot be written yet. For an observe-only epic where Story 1 doesn't capture (so no derivation work is queued and the provider is never invoked), LHC's exported `createDeterministicProvider` is the minimal construction-valid provider that makes the lifecycle run for real. Let me apply the three fixes.\n\n**SV-001 + SV-002 in index.ts:** real default SDK config + real `--resume` selector + module-level durable thread-id memory (survives connector teardown)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49181,"cache_read_input_tokens":346319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49181},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e","uuid":"76c1c1db-bbe9-49a4-a93b-88564261a686","request_id":"req_011Cc2ZQ2XMoRUrpnhZiVPud"}
