{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Hy831NJti2PvNzqRXvYXDu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Addressed all three blocking verifier findings (SV-001/002/003) while keeping Story 1 scope. SV-001 (production path was a placeholder): removed the fail-closed `inferenceNotConfigured` default and the null `--resume` selector; `activate()`/`createConnector()` now default to a real, construction-valid observe-only SDK config (LHC's exported `createDeterministicProvider`, background mode) and a real `--resume` selector (resume the most-recent cwd thread). session_start now actually resolves/creates the thread and initializes LHC on the production path. The deterministic provider is a documented interim: Epic 1 is observe-only and Story 1 does not capture yet (message_end is a no-op), so no derivation work is queued and the provider is never invoked — a real *completing* `ModelCall` cannot be written until `@earendil-works/pi-ai` becomes a build dependency (Story 5). SV-002 (reload used closure memory): moved the resolved thread id to MODULE scope (`rememberedSessionThreadId`, with `resetSessionThreadMemory()` test seam) so it survives the connector teardown a reload performs; the reload path reconstructs from it, kept across a reload and cleared on any other teardown; the reload test now uses two FRESH connectors sharing that durable memory. SV-003 (no title): connector-created threads now carry a default title `defaultThreadTitle(cwd)` (the cwd leaf), passed through `resolveThread` to `newThread`; tests assert cwd AND title. Also fixed a side effect the new real default introduced (the smoke test would have written `~/.lhc`) by redirecting it to a temp store. Tests now exercise the production connector path with real defaults (only environment overrides injected) for AC-1.1/1.2/1.7, plus a `parseLaunchFlags` unit test for the real launch source. All pi-lhc gates green (31 tests); lhc verify green (388).\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts\", \"reason\": \"A-8: `ambiguous_thread_id` caller-error code for partial-id resolve ambiguity (unchanged this turn).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/registry.ts\", \"reason\": \"A-8: cwd column (migration v2 + migrate-on-read), prefix/cwd-filtered selects, deterministic created_at,rowid ordering (unchanged this turn).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"A-8: cwd on NewThreadInput/ThreadInfo, partial-id resolve, cwd-filtered listThreads (unchanged this turn).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"A-8 registry tests (11), unchanged this turn.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\", \"reason\": \"initInstance (validate thread, force background mode) + disposeInstance (flush-on-dispose), unchanged this turn.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\", \"reason\": \"SV-003: new-thread creation now sets `title: deps.newThreadTitle ?? defaultThreadTitle(cwd)`; added exported `defaultThreadTitle(cwd)` (cwd leaf) and `newThreadTitle?` on ResolveDeps. Plus resolveThread modes + parseLaunchFlags from before.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\", \"reason\": \"pickThread cwd-scoped list + injectable selection (unchanged this turn).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"SV-001: replaced placeholder `inferenceNotConfigured` with real `defaultBuildSdkConfig` (deterministic observe-only SDK) and `defaultSelectThread` (most-recent --resume). SV-002: moved reload id to module-level `rememberedSessionThreadId` (survives connector teardown) with exported `resetSessionThreadMemory()`; reload reconstructs from it; onDispose keeps it only on reload, clears otherwise. Updated activate() doc.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Rewrote TC-1.1 to drive the PRODUCTION connector path (real default config + selector, only env overrides), asserting cwd + title + background instance + no orphan capture; kept TC-1.4 (flush+reattach).\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Added production-connector tests for TC-1.2 (resolve existing, no second thread) and TC-1.7 (--resume default selector); rewrote the reload test (SV-002) to use two fresh connectors sharing durable module memory + a non-reload-clears test; added a no-flag-title test (SV-003) and a parseLaunchFlags unit test; fixed the stale 'no title' comment.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Redirected the hook-routing test's connector to a temp store so the now-real default does not write ~/.lhc; reset module memory per test. (init/dispose real-behavior block from the prior turn retained.)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Re-recorded for the verifier-directed updates to the two Story 1 lifecycle test files.\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts: TC-1.1 (production connector path: cwd+title+background), TC-1.4 (flush+reattach) (2)\",\n      \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts: TC-1.6 resolver modes, parseLaunchFlags, no-flag title, TC-1.7 picker, TC-1.5 restart, TC-1.2 connector, TC-1.7 connector --resume, TC-1.3 plain-data, TC-1.5 fresh-connector reload, non-reload-clears (10)\",\n      \"packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts: A-8 registry cwd/partial-id/ambiguous/cwd-filter/most-recent/migrate-on-read (11)\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts: init/dispose block → real fail-closed behavior; hook-routing test redirected to a temp store (no ~/.lhc writes)\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 31,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 12\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter lhc verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter lhc green-verify\", \"result\": \"fail\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"SV-001: production activate/session_start now runs the real lifecycle — `defaultBuildSdkConfig` constructs a real background SDK (no early fail-closed return) and `defaultSelectThread` resolves a real --resume selection (most-recent cwd thread); tests drive the connector with these production defaults (only env overrides injected) for AC-1.1/1.2/1.7.\",\n      \"SV-002: reload reconstructs from durable state surviving teardown — the resolved id moved from the connector closure to module scope; the reload test now creates a FRESH connector after teardown and proves reconstruction with a no-flag launch and no duplicate; the id is kept only across a reload and cleared on other teardowns (covered by a dedicated test).\",\n      \"SV-003: connector-created fresh threads carry title metadata (`defaultThreadTitle(cwd)`); TC-1.1 and the reload/no-flag tests assert cwd AND title.\",\n      \"Caught a side effect the real default introduced: the smoke test's no-deps connector would have written the real ~/.lhc on session_start — redirected it to a temp store.\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"The Story-1 production provider is LHC's deterministic provider — an interim that makes the lifecycle real without a completing inference (impossible until @earendil-works/pi-ai is a build dependency). It is never invoked in Story 1 (no capture yet → no derivation work) and is replaced by the PI-auth `ModelCall` in Story 5.\",\n      \"--resume production selection is most-recent-in-cwd because the local PI type surface exposes only `ui.notify` (no interactive prompt); an operator picker awaits a PI input surface.\",\n      \"Reload durable id is in-process module state: it survives the reload teardown but is correctly dropped on process death (the next launch re-resolves) — no sidecar/mapping, consistent with epic I-1.\",\n      \"Pre-existing lhc green-verify immutability drift on packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts (file byte-unchanged vs HEAD but mismatching the manifest hash from the Epic 05 closeout) is unrelated to this story; lhc verify (build/typecheck/lint/boundaries + 388 tests) passes.\"\n    ],\n    \"openQuestions\": []\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Is LHC's deterministic provider acceptable as the Story-1 interim production provider for observe-only Epic 1 (never invoked in Story 1; replaced by the PI-auth ModelCall in Story 5)? A real completing inference is blocked on @earendil-works/pi-ai not yet being a build dependency.\",\n    \"Confirm against the real PI dependency: the launch-flag spelling for the named-session mode (--session vs --session-id) and whether a PI input surface exists for an interactive --resume picker (the default now resumes the most-recent cwd thread).\",\n    \"Title policy: the follow-up directed adding title metadata, so connector-created threads use the cwd leaf as a provisional creation-time title; TDQ Q4's richer derivation (e.g. first user prompt, Story 2+) remains deferred — confirm the cwd-leaf default is acceptable until then.\",\n    \"Pre-existing lhc immutability drift on packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts makes `pnpm --filter lhc green-verify` fail at the immutability step independent of this story; should it be re-baselined (out of this story's scope; not touched here)?\"\n  ],\n  \"specDeviations\": [\n    \"Production SDK provider for Story 1 is LHC's deterministic provider (interim), not the PI-auth-backed ModelCall (Story 5) — the completing-inference package (@earendil-works/pi-ai) is not yet a build dependency. Documented; the provider is never invoked in Story 1 because capture (Story 2) is not wired.\",\n    \"--resume production selection defaults to the most-recent cwd-scoped thread (no interactive input surface in the local PI types yet); the picker module remains fully cwd-scoped/titled and selection-injectable.\",\n    \"Reload reconstruction uses module-level in-process state for the durable resolved id (survives the reload teardown; dropped on process death) rather than a PI-session→thread mapping or a recovery sidecar (epic I-1).\",\n    \"resolveThread/pickThread take injected deps (cwd, registryPath, new-thread file path/title, selection) rather than the tech-design sketch's `(launch, pi: ExtensionAPI)` / `(cwd)` — ExtensionAPI carries none of those.\",\n    \"New thread title at creation = cwd leaf (`defaultThreadTitle`), a provisional Story-1 label; richer derivation is the deferred TDQ Q4.\",\n    \"A-8 added `ambiguous_thread_id` to lhc ErrorCode and a registry v2 migration (cwd) with migrate-on-read (carried from the initial implementation).\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Re-verify Story 1. Then proceed to Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation) on the lifecycle seam. When @earendil-works/pi-ai and the PI extension packages become build dependencies, replace the deterministic interim provider with the PI-auth ModelCall (Story 5) and wire an interactive --resume picker; optionally re-baseline the unrelated lhc retirement.test.ts manifest entry.\"\n}"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5212,"cache_read_input_tokens":462707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5212},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e","uuid":"96a3d34b-41f5-407f-9759-623988a39bb0","request_id":"req_011Cc2aLGidz5rkUX8pcjucT"}
